14. The role of AI-powered EHS software in construction safety
Construction safety management becomes more difficult as the number of subcontractors, work locations, permits and inspection activities increases.

Information may be spread across spreadsheets, paper forms, email approvals and separate contractor systems.

This fragmentation can delay corrective action and reduce management visibility.

An integrated EHS platform can connect operational safety activities.

For example, an inspection finding involving missing edge protection can be linked to a hazard record, assigned to a responsible person, escalated where appropriate and verified before closure.

AI-assisted analytics may help identify repeated findings, overdue actions or unusual patterns across projects.

However, AI-generated insights must be reviewed by competent personnel. The software does not itself determine legal compliance or replace required physical safeguards.

